  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The Diagrammatics of \u2018Race\u2019 (2024), published by Open Book Publishers, has been cited 8 times. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 3,393 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The Diagrammatics of \u2018Race\u2019 by Marianne Sommer was published by Open Book Publishers in 2024. Conceptually, the work connects to Kinship, Family tree, Race (biology), Humanity and Ideology. The book was recognised: ACLS Open Access Book Prize & Arcadia Open Access Publishing Award finalist (2026) \u2014 Anthropology.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 8 citations. Citations peaked in 2026 with 6 citing works. Notable citing venues include Evolutionary Biology/Evolutionary biology, History, philosophy and theory of the life sciences and NTM Zeitschrift f\u00fcr Geschichte der Wissenschaften Technik und Medizin. The citing works include 5 book chapters and 3 journal articles. They come from 6 countries, led by Germany, the United States and Austria.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 3,393 times via Google Books and OAPEN. It is recorded in 2 library collections.</p>",
